  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered estimates as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. A positive signed estimate supports the registered direction, and a negative signed estimate opposes it. For clinically meaningful magnitude, I used a 10% relative-difference threshold on the absolute overall mean of each dependency outcome. KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 robustness: H23 batch_a interaction estimate +0.021, interval -0.031 to +0.072. This is smaller than the main effect of about +0.796 and uncertain, so it neither demonstrates positive batch_a amplification nor excludes it; I leave it unresolved and deferred. H26 lineage interaction estimate -0.012, interval -0.057 to +0.033, and H27 STK11-loss interaction estimate -0.026, interval -0.079 to +0.026, also show no robust positive interaction and are small relative to the KEAP1 main effect. H28 STK11-loss main effect on NFE2L2 estimate -0.007, below the NFE2L2 threshold and interval-crossing, provides a useful specificity control against a simple STK11-confounding explanation. Taken together, these audits do not strongly undermine H18, so I request independent validation of H18. SMARCA2/SMARCA4: H29 batch_a interaction is statistically and practically meaningful but opposite to the registered direction: signed estimate -0.051, interval -0.095 to -0.007, beyond the SMARCA2 threshold of about 0.0415. This suggests that the SMARCA4-loss effect on SMARCA2 dependency is attenuated in batch_a, not absent overall. I reject H29 as stated but register a reversed interaction claim and a batch_a-specific mean-effect follow-up. H33 ARID1A-loss effect in SMARCA4-intact cells is small and interval-crossing, so it is rejected and closed. H34 SMARCA4-loss effect in ARID1A-intact cells is enormous and precise, supporting the specificity of the SMARCA4/SMARCA2 paralog signal and strengthening confidence in H7 pending validation. USP7/TP53: H25 adenocarcinoma effect is large and precise, +0.799, interval +0.776 to +0.823, supporting the validated TP53-loss/USP7 association in the dominant lineage. H30 batch_a interaction is negative and uncertain; it does not evidence positive batch_a amplification, so I leave it unresolved but deferred because H12 is already validated. WRN/MSI-high: H24 adenocarcinoma effect is large and precise, +0.784, interval +0.748 to +0.820, supporting H13. KRAS and EGFR adenocarcinoma refinements: H19 estimate +0.0115 and H20 estimate +0.0198, both below their respective 10% outcome thresholds and interval-crossing, including threshold-level possibilities. These remain unresolved and deferred because neither the overall nor the adenocarcinoma effects provide clinically compelling evidence. All conclusions remain dataset associations, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence state: validated accepted overall effect H12 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency. Unvalidated accepted overall effects: H7 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H13 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency, H18 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Robustness updates: H18 audits are reassuring: H23 batch interaction positive but uncertain; H26 lineage interaction negative/uncertain; H27 STK11 interaction negative/uncertain; H28 STK11 main effect null-like, arguing against broad STK11 confounding. Therefore validation requested for H18. H7 specificity: H34 SMARCA4-loss effect in ARID1A-intact cells remains huge; H33 ARID1A-loss effect in SMARCA4-intact cells is null. However H29 shows significant opposite batch_a interaction: SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 effect is attenuated in batch_a by about 0.051, beyond threshold. Registered reversed interaction and batch_a mean-effect follow-up. H13/WRN: H24 adenocarcinoma subgroup effect remains huge, supporting context independence from lineage subtype. H12/USP7: H25 adenocarcinoma subgroup effect remains huge; H30 batch interaction null-like. Unresolved borderline effects: H1/H19 KRAS and H3/H20 EGFR remain below threshold with intervals including threshold; deferred. Rejected/closed: H2 BRAF, H4 ERBB2, H5 original KEAP1 direction, H8 overall ARID1A, H9 MYC-POLR2A, H14 RB1-KIF18A, H28 STK11-NFE2L2, H33 ARID1A-SMARCA2 in SMARCA4-intact, H29 original batch interaction direction. Deferred/active: H1, H3, H6 MDM2, H10/H11 MYC effects, H15 KRAS-STAT3, H16 EGFR-RIT1, H17 ERBB2-TMED10, H21/H32 MDM2 lineage follow-up, H31 KRAS lineage interaction, and several unresolved audit interactions. Next analysis priorities: run batch_a SMARCA4-loss mean effect; optionally reverse interaction validation; maybe H31/H32/H21 if still resources; consider validation of H7 or H13 after H18 validation returns.",
  "validate": "H18"
