  "narrative": "Current priority is to extend and localize the newly accepted CDKN2A-loss finding and to complete biological/technical characterization of the core accepted associations. Estimates will be interpreted as already signed to the registered direction; positive values support the registered claim. Practical 10% thresholds remain approximately USP7 0.0093, MDM2 0.0269, KRAS 0.0245, and RIT1 0.0256. First, I test TP53 loss and weaker USP7 dependency among KEAP1-intact cells. The complementary KEAP1-loss stratum was accepted (H43), and the overall TP53/USP7 association was independently validated (H12), so the KEAP1-intact complement is needed to establish that the effect is not restricted to or driven only by KEAP1-loss cells. Second, I refine H96, the strongest new signal: CDKN2A loss among TP53-intact cells is associated with much stronger MDM2 dependency. A low 9p21 copy-number stratum is a plausible proxy for CDKN2A/p14ARF locus deletion, so I test whether the stronger MDM2 dependency is concentrated there. I also test whether MTAP loss, often co-deleted with CDKN2A, further distinguishes CDKN2A-loss cells, because locus co-deletion may indicate a more complete functional disruption of the 9p21 regulatory module. These are mechanistic refinements, not external causal claims. Third, I open two coherent bypass-oriented hypotheses that have not yet been tested: STK11 loss in KRAS-mutant cells may reduce dependence on mutant KRAS through alternative growth/survival signaling, and PIK3CA mutation in KRAS-wildtype cells may bypass upstream RIT1 input by activating downstream PI3K signaling. I register the latter as weaker RIT1 dependency. These proposals are intended to be analyzed alongside H97-H100, which already test non-Avana and adenocarcinoma robustness for the MDM2/CDKN2A signal and PIK3CA/KRAS-WT dependency. If H97 and H98 remain positive, the next appraise stage should strongly consider independent validation of H96 or the most biologically specific refinement. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset; they are not causal or externally generalizable until independently supported.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 explore priorities: core accepted associations are SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2; TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7; KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2; MSI-high -> much stronger WRN overall/adeno/BRCA2-intact/high TMB. H96 is accepted and active: CDKN2A loss in TP53-intact cells -> much stronger MDM2 dependency, signed discovery +0.119 (+0.079 to +0.158), MDM2 threshold ~0.027. Need robustness: non-Avana H97, adenocarcinoma H98. New proposed mechanistic refinements: low 9p21 copy stratum and MTAP co-deletion within CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact cells. Also complete TP53/USP7 by testing KEAP1-intact complement. Add two bypass predictors: STK11 loss among KRAS-mutant cells for weaker KRAS, and PIK3CA mutation among KRAS-wildtype cells for weaker RIT1. Avoid further broad NF1/KRAS follow-up after failed validation. Pending active broad claims can be deferred if they crowd analysis selection, but do not over-defer high-value accepted-effect complements. All estimates already signed; direction +1 is weaker dependency for loss-of-function/predictor if hypothesis is bypass, direction -1 is stronger dependency. Accept only if interval supports practical 10% threshold."
