  "narrative": "I registered seven refinements that together should complete the most informative set of currently active tests when combined with H42, H106, H107, H108, and H109. All returned estimates will be interpreted as already signed to the registered direction. For the new direction -1 hypotheses, a positive signed value supports the registered claim: for MDM2 or SMARCA2, a negative raw exposed-minus-comparator difference means cells in the exposed group have a more negative, hence stronger, dependency score. For interaction contrasts with direction -1, a positive signed value means the exposed-comparator effect is more negative in the indicated subgroup than in its complement. The main practical thresholds remain approximately MDM2 0.0269 and SMARCA2 0.0415, corresponding to 10 percent of the absolute outcome means.\n\nThe primary focus remains localization and robustness of the validated CDKN2A-loss signal in TP53-intact cells (H96), not a causal claim. First, I register the effect within screen_batch batch_a to assess technical batch robustness. A positive signed result would indicate that the stronger MDM2 dependency associated with CDKN2A loss is present in the largest screen batch; a null or reversed result would raise a batch-specific technical concern. Second, I test the same association in a high-9p21-copy stratum and register a low-versus-high 9p21 interaction. H102 found support in the low-copy stratum, but that alone cannot determine whether CDKN2A loss matters generally or only in cells with nearby locus deletion. If the high-copy effect remains substantial and the interaction is near null, the CDKN2A association is not driven exclusively by low 9p21 copy number. If the interaction is strongly positive, the effect may be concentrated in deletion-like genomic contexts. Third, I test CDKN2A loss among TP53-intact and MTAP-intact cells, and register an MTAP-loss interaction. Because MTAP is often co-deleted with CDKN2A, persistence of the CDKN2A effect when MTAP is intact would argue against the effect being purely a marker of broader 9p21 co-deletion. A strong MTAP-loss interaction would support a locus-co-deletion modifier. The active broad MTAP H106 and CDKN2A-intact MTAP H107, plus the active TP53-loss complement H108 and TP53-loss interaction H109, complete this localization.\n\nI also add two comparisons that test whether the accepted synthetic-lethality pattern is pathway-specific rather than a generic predictor effect. First, SMARCA4 loss is tested among TP53-loss cells for stronger SMARCA2 dependency. This checks whether the validated SMARCA4 synthetic lethality remains in the p53-disrupted context, where the TP53/USP7 and CDKN2A/MDM2 effects are particularly relevant. Second, CDKN2A loss is tested against SMARCA2 dependency among TP53-intact cells. This is a specificity control for H96: if CDKN2A loss produces a similarly large change in SMARCA2, the MDM2 association could partly reflect a shared genomic or synthetic-lethality confounder rather than a pathway-selective signal. A null or small SMARCA2 result, together with the large MDM2 result, would support MDM2-specificity. These remain association tests in the supplied data, not causal or generalizable mechanisms. The active H42 KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 test in EGFR-amplification-positive cells remains high priority for completing the validated oxidative-stress pathway robustness set.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 explore. Current validated/accepted in-supplied-set associations: SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2; TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7; KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2; MSI-high -> much stronger WRN overall and adenocarcinoma-supported; CDKN2A loss in TP53-intact -> much stronger MDM2. Practical 10% thresholds: MDM2 about 0.0269, SMARCA2 about 0.0415, USP7/NFE2L2 about 0.0093, WRN about 0.0301. Direction convention: for direction -1, positive signed estimate = stronger dependency (raw score more negative); for direction +1, positive signed estimate = weaker dependency (raw score less negative).\n\nPriorities now: analyze exactly the active set H42, H106, H107, H108, H109 plus the seven new proposals if analysis slots allow. Localize H96 by batch_a robustness, high-9p21 stratum, low-vs-high 9p21 interaction, MTAP-intact CDKN2A effect, and MTAP-loss interaction. Also analyze SMARCA4 effect in TP53-loss cells and CDKN2A effect on SMARCA2 as specificity/control for the MDM2 claim. If H96 remains robust across these strata, strengthen the conclusion that CDKN2A loss with intact TP53 is specifically associated with stronger MDM2 dependency. If effects vanish under MTAP-intact or TP53-loss conditions, interpret as context- or locus-dependent association. Do not interpret as causation or external generalizability."
}

