  "narrative": "All returned signed estimates were interpreted using registered directions: for direction -1, positive means stronger dependency in exposed cells; for direction +1, positive means weaker dependency. Practical 10%-scale thresholds used were approximately 0.0269 for MDM2 and 0.0093 for USP7/NFE2L2.\n\nH154 and H156 show that CDKN2A loss remains associated with stronger MDM2 dependency in both high and low research signature A: H154 signed effect 0.158 (95% CI 0.071 to 0.244), H156 signed effect 0.098 (95% CI 0.033 to 0.164). Both exclude null and clear the MDM2 threshold, so I accept both and close them. Because the direct mean difference is robust in both tails of signature A, H151 (a high-signature-A interaction) is closed unresolved; the interaction itself remains imprecise and is not established as modification.\n\nH155 and H157 show that KEAP1 loss remains associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency in both high and low research signature B: signed effects 0.816 (95% CI 0.777 to 0.854) and 0.751 (95% CI 0.711 to 0.791). Both clear the USP7/NFE2L2 threshold by a large margin, so they are accepted and closed. H152 is likewise closed unresolved as an interaction; the broad driver effect is robust, but signature-B modification is not supported by the interaction estimate.\n\nH158 localizes CDKN2A loss to stronger MDM2 dependency in TP53-loss cells restricted to low-copy 9p21: signed effect 0.201 (95% CI 0.098 to 0.304). This excludes null and clears the MDM2 threshold, so I accept it with caution because the comparator cell is only 21 and this is a narrow post-selected deletion-like genomic context. It refines the broad CDKN2A-MDM2 association rather than proving causality or generalizability.\n\nThe specificity/crosstalk tests did not produce new accepted driver associations. H162 is the clearest null: CDKN2A loss in MSI-high-negative cells has signed effect 0.005 (95% CI -0.014 to 0.025), with the entire practical range below the WRN threshold, so I reject it. H159, H160, H161, and H163 are not supported: KEAP1 loss did not robustly predict USP7 in TP53/CDKN2A-intact cells, TP53 loss did not robustly predict NFE2L2 in KEAP1/CDKN2A-intact cells, KEAP1 loss did not robustly predict MDM2 in TP53/CDKN2A-intact cells, and research marker F did not robustly modify the KEAP1-NFE2L2 interaction. Their intervals are either opposite to the registered direction or imprecise enough that some clinically meaningful values remain possible, so I close them unresolved rather than claiming exact nulls. Overall, the main accepted dataset associations remain unchanged, and no new causal or broadly generalizable mechanism can be inferred.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 appraise after H154-H163. Validation budget remains exhausted; all future evidence is discovery only unless scheduled. Accepted direct localizations: H154 CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 in high research signature A; H156 CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 in low research signature A; H155 KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 in high research signature B; H157 KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 in low research signature B; H158 CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 in TP53-loss low-copy 9p21, accepted with caution due small comparator cell. H151 and H152 are closed unresolved because direct effects are robust across high/low signature tails while the interaction estimates are imprecise. Specificity tests: H162 CDKN2A-WRN in MSI-negative rejected as practically null; H159-H161 and H163 closed unresolved due no robust support but intervals not excluding some meaningful values. Major accepted in-dataset associations remain: KEAP1 loss with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency; TP53 loss with much weaker USP7 dependency; SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency; CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency across many accepted contexts. Major unsupported/rejected include direct MTAP effects independent of CDKN2A-loss context, most constructed marker/signature direct interactions, EGFR amplification as EGFR predictor, KRAS mutation broad effect, NF1-KRAS after validation, and BRAF/ERBB2 driver-receptor expectations. Newly proposed next active set: direct WRN-MSI and USP7-TP53 mean differences in high and low research signature C to test whether arbitrary signature C localizes accepted robust drivers. Treat all conclusions as dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims. Practical thresholds: MDM2 about 0.0269, USP7/NFE2L2 about 0.0093, WRN about 0.0301, SMARCA2 about 0.0415; require CI excluding null and clearing threshold before acceptance."
