+0.030, -0.038 to +0.098), so H197 is unresolved and closed. ERBB2 amplification among EGFR-negative cells does not support clinically meaningful weaker EGFR dependency; the estimate is near zero with an interval that still barely includes the practical threshold, so H198 is unresolved but closed rather than claimed. SMARCA4 loss is specifically linked to SMARCA2, not to STAT3 or POLR2A: H199 and H200 reject meaningful stronger dependency because their upper bounds fall below the approximate outcome thresholds. Overall, the new results reinforce specificity of the accepted PTEN-STAT3, SMARCA4-SMARCA2, KEAP1-NFE2L2, TP53-USP7, MSI-WRN, and CDKN2A-MDM2 associations while rejecting most new direct or tail-stratified associations as unsupported or too imprecise in this supplied lung-lineage dataset.",
