  "narrative": "Assessing newly delivered discovery evidence with validation capacity exhausted, so no independent validation was requested. I used the signed-direction convention: for direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger/more negative dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker/less negative dependency. I judged scientific and practical meaningfulness using the operational ~0.10 dependency-score-unit threshold used in prior stages, interval exclusion of zero, and valid cell counts. H250-H257 are all accepted and closed: SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 dependency remains very large under high screen_roc_auc (+0.791 [0.764,0.819]), high Cas9 activity (+0.791 [0.759,0.823]), and low aneuploidy (+0.799 [0.759,0.838]); TP53-loss USP7 dependency remains very large under high screen quality (+0.806 [0.780,0.832]) and high Cas9 activity (+0.799 [0.768,0.829]); KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency remains very large under high screen quality (+0.793 [0.764,0.822]) and high aneuploidy (+0.796 [0.755,0.838]); and MSI-high WRN dependency remains very large under high screen quality (+0.790 [0.751,0.829]). These do not rescue the associations mechanistically, but they reduce concern that these large supplied-dataset effects are explained by screen noise, low Cas9 editing efficiency, or high copy-number burden alone. H258-H260 are accepted and closed: PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency is robust to both high and low screen quality and to high Cas9 activity, with estimates +0.253 [0.181,0.325], +0.280 [0.205,0.355], and +0.263 [0.183,0.344]. Because PTEN-STAT3 remains accepted internally but lacks independent validation, this robustness to assay-quality and editing-efficiency strata strengthens it as a dataset-specific association, while still leaving open correlated biology, genetic co-occurrence, copy-number effects, or other residual confounders. H261 is accepted and closed with caution: CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2 dependency in TP53-intact cells under high Cas9 activity has point estimate +0.132 [0.068,0.196], above the ~0.10 threshold and excluding zero, although the lower bound is slightly below the threshold. This is consistent with the validated TP53-intact CDKN2A-MDM2 effect and does not support attenuation due to editing inefficiency. All conclusions are association-level in the supplied lung-lineage dataset and do not establish causality, therapeutic relevance, or external generalizability. Because validation capacity is exhausted, newly registered proposals focus on additional internal confounding/robustness tests of the unvalidated PTEN-STAT3 association and completion of low-aneuploidy strata for two large validated associations.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 21 appraise state. Validation capacity exhausted. Due results H250-H261 all valid and accepted; investigations closed. Major supported dataset associations now have robustness evidence across screen quality, Cas9 activity, and aneuploidy strata: SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2; TP53-loss weaker USP7; KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2; MSI-high stronger WRN. PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 is now robust to high/low screen quality and high Cas9 activity (+0.253 to +0.280), but still lacks independent validation and remains association-level. CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2 in TP53-intact high-Cas9 cells accepted with caution: point +0.132 [0.068,0.196]. Future internal analyses should focus on PTEN-STAT3 across media, culture type, library, ploidy, omics completeness, and batch, and complete low-aneuploidy tests for TP53-USP7 and KEAP1-NFE2L2. No causal or external generalizability claims. Remaining key uncertainty: unvalidated PTEN-STAT3 residual confounding, small-cell CDKN2A-MDM2 interactions, and multiplicity."
