{
  "narrative": "No new validation response is due and independent validation capacity is exhausted. The final synthesis therefore assesses the accumulated discovery and prior validation evidence for the supplied 2000-sample lung adenocarcinoma-like dataset. Because dependency scores are continuous with standard deviations about 0.18-0.26, I treated roughly 0.10 dependency-score units (about 0.4-0.5 SD for many scores) together with valid Welch cells and interval exclusion of zero as scientifically meaningful, consistent with the stated 10% practical threshold. Signed estimates follow the registered hypothesis direction. Supported dataset-specific associations. KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H18/H5; R5 +0.796 [0.776,0.816], validated R26 +0.781 [0.752,0.809]) and persists in low screen_roc_auc (R277) and low Cas9 strata (R283). TP53 loss is associated with much weaker USP7 dependency (H12; R10 +0.802 [0.782,0.822], validated R13 +0.797 [0.769,0.824]), robust in low screen_roc_auc (R276) and low Cas9 strata (R282). SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H7; R7 +0.784 [0.765,0.803], validated R39 +0.807 [0.777,0.838]), robust in low screen_roc_auc (R275) and low Cas9 strata (R281). MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency (H13; R11 +0.790 [0.760,0.819], validated R53 +0.771 [0.720,0.822]), including adenocarcinoma subtype (H24; R23/R40), low screen_roc_auc (R278), and low Cas9 strata (R284), though the latter has only 27 exposed cells and is accepted with caution. CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, clearest in TP53-intact cells (H96; R70 +0.119 [0.079,0.158], validated R93 +0.122 [0.064,0.180]) and overall (H117; R108 +0.117 [0.082,0.152]); low screen_roc_auc and low Cas9 checks remain positive but attenuated (H278 R279 +0.103, H279 R280 +0.106, H284 R285 +0.105), with lower bounds often below 0.10, so magnitude in degraded-quality subsets is uncertain. PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency (H184; R188 +0.267 [0.215,0.319]); although independently validated PTEN-STAT3 has not been obtained because validation capacity is exhausted, the association is internally robust across many strata, including TP53 status, KRAS status, MYC expression, IFN and EMT signatures, ploidy, media, culture, omics completeness, batch A, low screen_roc_auc, and low Cas9 (H285; R286 +0.372 [0.268,0.476]). Negative or non-meaningful findings. Direct target associations are generally null or far below the practical threshold: KRAS mutation with dependency_KRAS (H1; R1 +0.014 [-0.004,0.031], validated R80 +0.001), BRAF V600E with dependency_BRAF (H2; R2 -0.017), EGFR amplification with dependency_EGFR (H3; R3 +0.025 and validated H51/R133 -0.027), and ERBB2 amplification with dependency_ERBB2 (H4; R4 +0.001). MYC amplification is not practically associated with POLR2A, RPL11, DHX9, KIF18A, TMED10, or WRN; the nominally significant WRN effect (R186 -0.033 [-0.064,-0.002]) is small. RB1 loss is not practically associated with KIF18A or POLR2A, NF1 loss fails independent validation for dependency_KRAS in KRAS-wild-type cells (R52 discovery +0.039, R66 validation +0.000), MTAP loss is not a robust modifier of CDKN2A-MDM2, and high/low copy_number_9p21 or batch strata are wide or boundary-like. Constructed research markers D/E/F and signatures A/B/C show no meaningful dependency associations beyond nominal small effects; some intervals exclude zero but point estimates are below 0.10. Unresolved uncertainty. The main remaining registered active evidence gap is the low screen_nnmd robustness battery H286-H292, which has no evidence yet. These include PTEN-STAT3, SMARCA4-SMARCA2, TP53-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, MSI-high-WRN, overall CDKN2A-MDM2, and TP53-intact CDKN2A-MDM2 in lower-quartile screen_nnmd. Additional unresolved or bounded uncertainty concerns CDKN2A-MDM2 effects in TP53-loss or MTAP/9p21 interactions (e.g., H108 validation R106 lower bound approximately zero), non-Avana PTEN-STAT3 (H265 underpowered), and small or nominal interaction estimates. PTEN-STAT3 remains accepted only as a robust association within the supplied data, not as externally validated or causal. Most informative next analysis is to run the active low screen_nnmd battery H286-H292. Persistence of intervals excluding zero with estimates at least about 0.10 would further strengthen dataset-specific robustness across degraded screen noise; attenuation or invalid cells would keep the claims association-level and specify that screen noise can limit inference. All accepted claims should be interpreted as associations within this single supplied lung adenocarcinoma-like dataset, not as causal mechanisms or generalizable clinical biology.",
